# Keep these out of the image build context: personal data, build artifacts, the repository, docs and the READMEs.
# Exactly three files come back in (the ! lines at the end, which must stay below the docs line): docs/en, docs/ja and
# docs/zh-CN/changelog.md, which the nginx image build reads for the About page.
# The compose files and .env live in docker/, which is not needed inside an image. backend/, ai-service/, frontend/ and nginx/ stay in:
# each Dockerfile copies only what its image needs (ai-service/Dockerfile also reuses two build scripts from backend/).
**/data
**/data-ai
**/progress.json
**/*.xlsx
**/*.xls
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.sqlite*
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/target
**/.vite
.claude
**/.env
**/.env.*
.git
docker
.dockerignore
.github
docs
scripts
tests
tools
README.md
README
!docs/en/changelog.md
!docs/ja/changelog.md
!docs/zh-CN/changelog.md
